medical-chemistry-tab = Medical synthesis
medical-chemistry-instructions = Transfer precursor from the beaker into the buffer on the Input tab. Select a medicine, protocol and batch volume. Finished medicine returns to the buffer for packaging.
medical-chemistry-amount = Feedstock volume, units (1–60):
medical-chemistry-protocol-rapid = Rapid synthesis — volume and speed
medical-chemistry-protocol-precision = Precision synthesis — purity and potency
medical-chemistry-protocol-purify = Purify finished medicine
medical-chemistry-description-rapid = 12 seconds within the operating range. 100% yield, 80% base purity. Useful when speed and quantity matter; bound impurities cause a toxic load.
medical-chemistry-description-precision = 28 seconds within the operating range. 90% yield, 99% base purity. Slower, with more active medicine per dose and fewer impurities.
medical-chemistry-description-purify = 20 seconds within the operating range. Uses finished medicine from the buffer. Removes bound impurities and loses 5% of the active ingredient; recovered volume depends on initial purity. Overheating worsens the result.
medical-chemistry-preview = Without overheating: { $volume } units at { $purity }% purity. Operating range: { $min }–{ $max } °C. Reaction time: { $seconds } s, plus warm-up.
medical-chemistry-analysis = BUFFER ANALYSIS
    { $precursor }: { $raw } units.
    { $medicine }: { $volume } units; average purity { $purity }%.
medical-chemistry-purity-help = Purity determines healing strength. Bound impurities cause a toxic load and require purification rather than ordinary separation. Overdose thresholds still use the full medicine volume.
medical-chemistry-start = Start processing
medical-chemistry-cancel = Abort and return feedstock to buffer
medical-chemistry-heat-automatic = Thermostat
medical-chemistry-heat-boost = Boost heating
medical-chemistry-heat-cool = Cooling
medical-chemistry-thermal-help = The thermostat maintains the centre of the operating range. Boost heating shortens warm-up but must be switched off. Below the range, synthesis stops; above it, synthesis slows and the batch accumulates irreversible thermal contamination. Processing pauses without power.
medical-chemistry-readout = REACTOR: { $temperature } °C • feedstock { $volume } units
    Progress { $progress }% • thermal contamination { $stress }%
medical-chemistry-status-ready = Ready to load a batch
medical-chemistry-status-running = Processing batch
medical-chemistry-status-complete = Batch ready — check the buffer and package the medicine
medical-chemistry-status-cancelled = Processing aborted; feedstock returned
medical-chemistry-status-unpowered = No power — processing paused
medical-chemistry-batch-name = { $name } ({ $purity }%)
medical-chemistry-scan-purity = Batch purity: { $purity }%.
reagent-name-bicaridine-precursor = bicaridine precursor
reagent-name-dermaline-precursor = dermaline precursor
reagent-name-dexalin-precursor = dexalin precursor
reagent-desc-medical-precursor = An unfinished pharmaceutical base. Requires medical synthesis in a ChemMaster. Has no healing effect and is toxic when administered.
guide-entry-eclipse-medical-chemistry = Medical synthesis and purity
medical-chemistry-protocol-personalize = Patient-specific formulation from an assayed sample
medical-chemistry-description-personalize = 18 seconds of reaction time. Uses finished medicine and an assayed patient reference in the separate slot. 95% yield; starting purity is retained. Therapeutic affinity is 115% for the matching patient and 65% for others, with additional toxic load on mismatch. This is separate from blood compatibility.
medical-chemistry-reference-slot = Insert / eject reference sample
medical-chemistry-reference-ready = Assayed profile: { $profile }
medical-chemistry-reference-needed = Personalisation requires one unambiguous, laboratory-assayed patient reference.
medical-chemistry-personalized = Patient-specific profile { $profile }.
medical-chemistry-mixed-profiles = This medicine contains different patient profiles. Separate the batches on the Input tab before purification or personalisation.
medical-chemistry-analyzer-tab = Laboratory analysis
medical-chemistry-analyzer-instructions = Insert a beaker or vial in the input slot. Analysis reserves 5 units for 10 seconds. Assayed material returns to the buffer for bottling and transfer to the pharmaceutical synthesizer's reference slot. The instrument measures composition, purity and sample identity. Diagnoses and transfusion compatibility are studied separately.
medical-chemistry-analyze = Analyze 5 units of sample
medical-chemistry-assay-heading = LAST ANALYSIS RESULT
medical-chemistry-assay-readout = Analysis progress { $progress }% • sample in chamber { $volume } units
medical-chemistry-assay-compound = { $name }: { $volume } units at { $purity }% purity.
medical-chemistry-assay-no-profile = No unambiguous biological profile established. Chemical samples and mixed biological identities cannot be used for personalisation.
medical-chemistry-status-analyzing = Laboratory analysis in progress
medical-chemistry-status-assayed = Analysis complete — assayed material is in the buffer
medical-chemistry-status-warming = Warming up — reaction starts within the operating range
medical-chemistry-status-overheated = OVERHEATING — batch contamination increasing; switch to thermostat or cooling!
research-technology-pharmaceutical-laboratory = Pharmaceutical laboratory
ent-PharmaceuticalSynthesizer = pharmaceutical synthesizer
    .desc = A precision reactor for clinical precursors and patient-specific formulations. Personalisation requires an assayed patient reference.
ent-PharmaceuticalAnalyzer = pharmaceutical laboratory analyzer
    .desc = Measures compound composition and purity and assays biological references. Returns assayed material to its buffer.
ent-PharmaceuticalSynthesizerMachineCircuitboard = pharmaceutical synthesizer machine board
    .desc = A machine board for a pharmaceutical synthesizer.
ent-PharmaceuticalAnalyzerMachineCircuitboard = pharmaceutical analyzer machine board
    .desc = A machine board for a pharmaceutical laboratory analyzer.
ent-CratePharmaceuticalLaboratory = pharmaceutical laboratory equipment crate
    .desc = Analyzer and synthesizer boards, three vials and two large beakers. Machines require assembly.
